course: dictionary
lesson: 16102
title: One word, three meanings: weaving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word weaving can mean making cloth, a piece of woven cloth, or moving in and out between things. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: «Ada sat at the loom all afternoon, weaving a blue scarf.» The loom and the scarf are the clues. Weaving means making cloth by crossing threads over and under each other. Try your meaning in the sentence: "sat at the loom, making cloth by crossing threads" makes sense.
explain: «The little runner was weaving through the crowd to reach the bus.» There is no loom and no cloth here. Weaving means moving in and out between people, dodging around them. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Weaving is making cloth by crossing threads over and under each other on a loom.
fact: A weaving is a piece of cloth or art made this way, such as «The museum has a weaving of a sailing ship.»
fact: Weaving can also mean moving in and out between things, like a runner going around other people.
fact: Weave is the base verb: weave, weaves, wove or weaved, woven or weaved, and weaving is its -ing form.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Ada sat at the loom all afternoon, weaving a blue scarf.» What is weaving here? | Playing a tune on a flute | Cooking a meal | *Making cloth by crossing threads over and under | Painting a picture of the sea
exercise: «The bird spent a week weaving its nest from grass and twigs.» What does weaving mean here? | *Joining grass and twigs in and out to build the nest | Flying very fast | Sleeping in a tree | Singing loudly
exercise: «The little runner was weaving through the crowd.» What does weaving mean? | *Moving in and out between the people | Falling over | Shouting for help | Standing still
test: What is a loom for? | *Holding threads while you weave cloth | Storing coal | Cooking food | Catching fish
test: In «Her weaving won a prize», which word names the piece of art? | prize | *weaving | won | Her
exam: Which sentence uses weaving to mean moving in and out between things? | We ate our lunch | The loom was made of wood | The bird sang a happy song | *The cyclist was weaving between the parked cars
